+++ b/docs/pose-control/HANDOFF-2026-09-16.md
@@ -47,0 +48,4 @@ Precise numerical joint edits and redo should reuse the current geometry/history
+
+## Review correction: a newer reference operation wins
+
+The pose handoff now reuses the existing setup snapshot (reference epoch, pending count, recipe/selection identity and parent bindings) and refuses a reply while another setup operation is active. A new role-slot upload can begin before its filename changes: an unchanged source-pair snapshot alone is therefore insufficient. The render reply must not switch recipes and invalidate that newer upload. One native regression holds both requests, releases the guide first, then proves that the newer upload still attaches to the original recipe. Causal tests execute the actual handoff function with changed upload/epoch/picker state and a non-conflicting control. Identity fields additionally require strings rather than coercible arrays. None of this retries or cancels the user's newer operation.
